KINO licensing
==============

Copyright (c) 2026 KINO contributors

This repository contains software, open hardware source, and reserved brand
assets. They do not share one blanket license.

Software and general documentation
----------------------------------

Unless a path is listed below, repository files are licensed under the MIT
License. The complete text is in LICENSES/MIT.txt.

Open hardware source
--------------------

The following paths are licensed under the CERN Open Hardware Licence Version
2 - Strongly Reciprocal, CERN-OHL-S-2.0:

  hardware/**
  docs/HARDWARE.md
  kino_twin_spec/component-manifest.json
  kino_twin_spec/SOURCES.md

The complete unmodified text is in LICENSES/CERN-OHL-S-2.0.txt. This choice is
version 2 only, not "or any later version".

Reserved material
-----------------

The following paths are not distributed under MIT or CERN-OHL-S-2.0:

  docs/assets/brand/**
  docs/assets/product/**
  archive/**

The wordmarks and icons the applications ship are the same artwork, trimmed
and recoloured, so they carry the same terms. The MIT grant on apps/** does
not reach them:

  apps/studio/src/assets/**
  apps/twin/src/assets/**
  apps/roll-web/src/assets/**
  apps/studio/public/icon-*.png
  apps/twin/public/icon-*.png
  apps/roll-web/public/icon-*.png

Those files are marked LicenseRef-KINO-Reserved. See
LICENSES/LicenseRef-KINO-Reserved.txt.

Third-party files
-----------------

Two committed files are neither ours to license nor covered by the grants
above, and REUSE.toml overrides the blanket declaration on firmware/** for
both:

  firmware/p4/main/icons_w98.h              Microsoft Windows 98 shell icons,
                                            LicenseRef-Microsoft-Proprietary,
                                            no licence held
  firmware/c6/partitions_eh_cp_ota_4m.csv   Espressif Systems, Apache-2.0,
                                            text in LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt

Those annotations record ownership. They grant nothing. THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md
states what each one means for anyone distributing a build, including the
unresolved position on the icon artwork.

Trademark
---------

The licenses above do not grant permission to use the KINO name, KINO D4 name,
wordmarks, logos, or trade dress to imply endorsement or origin. See
TRADEMARKS.md.

Machine-readable scope
----------------------

REUSE.toml is the authoritative path map for automated license tooling. SPDX
identifiers in individual files override the path map where present.
